# Local denylist for the public-repo leak hooks (TEMPLATE — contains no real names).
#
# Two ways to supply the real private/other-project names to block:
#   1) git config hooks.denyListPath /path/to/private/denylist.txt   (recommended: a file
#      kept in a PRIVATE repo — single source of truth shared across your public repos)
#   2) copy this file to .githooks/deny-list.local (gitignored) and add names here.
#
# One extended-regex per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Keeping the real
# names ONLY outside version control ensures this PUBLIC repo's committed files never name
# a private project.
#
# Examples of the KINDS of patterns to add (replace with your own):
#   some-private-app
#   another-client-name
#   @somescope/
